															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/huitzil" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(375435); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=375435&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607266793" alt="Huitzil" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=375435)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/huitzil" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(375435); return false;" >Huitzil</a></span> <span class="odate time_1420937873 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Jan 2015 00:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2203206">
									

<p>&quot;It's Secure, Contain, Protect not Destroy, Destroy, Destroy&quot; is not an argument, it's a slogan, and it's not a particularly good one.</p>
<p>Securing, Containing and Protecting is not something that is undertaken for its own benefit; the things they do must be for SOME PURPOSE. That purpose is protecting human life from supernatural threats. Most of the time they do this by containing things. If they could do this by destroying something, and someone said &quot;We can't do this! We're not the Destroy, Destroy, Destroy Foundation!&quot; that person would be beaten unconscious with a pool cue.</p>
<p>And they AREN'T studying him. They are gaining no useful information from him. There is nothing to suggest they are attempting to gain useful information from him in the article, and on top of this, they NEVER gain any useful information from ANY SCP, ever, that has any application to anything beyond the containment of the SCP itself, because The SCP Has To Be Mysterious. (This is part of what makes them screamingly incompetent, how much science they can try to do while still learning nothing.)</p>
<p>And they don't know what his corpse will do? They don't know what ANYTHING will do EVER. Their total and fundamental incompetence at gaining information should render them incapable of any action, because when you have no idea what any of the rules are (and they have no idea what any of the rules are), all actions or lack of actions have the same chance of a terrible outcome. They don't know what he'll do when he's dead, but they don't know what he'll do when he stays alive tomorrow either. Since Bad Shit Happening follows no rules whatsoever, no action or lack of action can reduce the risk of Bad Shit Happening. If all actions have equal chances of catastrophe, take the action that is faster, cheaper, and doesn't involve torturing someone.</p>
<p>The fact the guy's condition is disintegrating and there's no tests yielding any information suggests they are not attempting to learn this information; as the condition is clearly killing him tortuously, if they cared about learning things from him, they'd be expediting that shit to get it done before he became unusable. They are not. There is nothing to indicate they are attempting to do so.</p>
<p>They are allowing a guy, a guy who the employees personally known, to be slowly and agonizingly tortured for no in-universe reason whatsoever, and the only out-of-universe reason is to allow the author to adhere to a stupid slogan.</p>

							</div>

								
					
