														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3605980">
									

<p>This is for sure not the first SCP that portrays Foundation denying euthanasia. It's just the way they go; they don't <em>provide</em> nor grant commodities until needed to fulfill their role. Euthanasia is part of that set. Why don't they kill the girl that bends reality? They even had to apply to get permission to kill the damn omnicidal lizard!</p>
<p>Author had the detail to even change the interviewer for someone evidently less related to Thompson (he treats him with its designation number) to acknowledge that the friendlier doctor probably couldn't bear it. That's fine writing there, not &quot;slogan adhesion&quot;.</p>
<p>As for the &quot;slogan&quot;, is part of the very first guideline you have to completely read in order to become a member. it's not a slogan. It's not even canon. It's METAcanon, part of how this site is thought about. The fact that this is +96 somewhat shows you're playing offbeat with this argument.</p>
<p>And last but not least, &quot;stupid&quot; is an adjective that adds nothing to discussion and needlessly makes one want to report you. Don't.</p>

							</div>

								
					
