					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1372582&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607266793" alt="Jacob Conwell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1372582)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;" >Jacob Conwell</a></span> <span class="odate time_1538691762 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Oct 2018 22:22</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4013992">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Also the fact that there was no test log at all to back up this scp.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I mean, the document implies that there is plenty of testing going on with SCP-2860, what with a solid list of marble types produced, materials not affected by the effect, and high-speed photography being used to determine how the transformations take place.</p>
<p>A test log is not included in the document provided on the site because a) I felt it was not necessary for the narrative being told (not every article has a test log) and b) such a test log would be fairly boring, as it would be different flavors of &quot;SCP-2860 touches X. X becomes/doesn't become marble.&quot;</p>
<p>These articles are designed to be entertaining snapshots of the Foundation, after all. Don't confuse artistic decisions out of universe for negligence in-universe.</p>
<p>As for why the Foundation doesn't destroy SCP-2860, well that's because that is not what they do. There are boatloads of SCPs that cause as much suffering/pain to the SCPs as SCP-2860 does, and are arguably more dangerous to have under lock and key.</p>
<p>If you don't like the portrayal of the Foundation here, that's fine. Downvote as you please. But you have a very long list of articles to hand a -1 if this is your reasoning for that.</p>

							</div>

								
					
