														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2201967">
									

<p>It's the Secure, Contain, Protect Foundation, not the Destroy, Destroy, Destroy Foundation. Anomalous things, by their nature, have information that can be gained from them. If they completely understood him, they would slap an -EX on the end of his SCP designation and then maybe kill him. Since there is still some information to be gained from him, they're keeping him alive to study how his anomalous effects affect him. For example, they might want to look into that &quot;feeling of a small static discharge.&quot; that he gets when he converts things - you can't interview him when he's dead.</p>

